# =============================================================================
# Store — MY-STORE requests (VS Code REST Client) — GET /api/v1/stores/my-store
# =============================================================================
# my-store resolves the CALLER's own store by storeAdminId = caller's publicId.
# No role gate — the DATA is the gate: a caller with no store gets an honest 404.
# This is the endpoint ROLE_STORE_MANAGER personas live on.
#
# How to run:
#   1. Start the backend: `docker compose up -d --build` — http://localhost:4000
#   2. Click the "Send Request" CodeLens above any request below.
#
# Prerequisites (TWO admin personas — see request 8 for why):
#   a) admin@devtunde.com — the working admin (same one as every other store
#      probe file). Promote with:
#        update users set role = 'ROLE_ADMIN' where email = 'admin@devtunde.com';
#   b) boss@devtunde.com — a DEDICATED admin who is NEVER assigned a store by
#      any probe file, so request 10's expected 404 stays stable no matter
#      which files ran before (review round 1 finding). Promote with:
#        update users set role = 'ROLE_ADMIN' where email = 'boss@devtunde.com';
#
# Notes:
#   - Run top-to-bottom on first use — later requests assume earlier ones ran.
#   - All data is FAKE. The automated suite: StoreApiTests (src/test/java).
#   - Access tokens expire after 15 MINUTES. If tokened requests suddenly 401,
#     re-send requests 2 (manager), 3 (admin) and 9 (boss) to refresh the chain.
#   - Re-running: requests 1, 8 and 11 return 409 (personas persist) — harmless.
#   - Expected codes: 200 own store, 401 no/invalid token, 404 no store,
#     405 wrong method, 204 delete.
# =============================================================================

@storeUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/stores
@authUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth

### 1 — Setup: signup the manager persona
# Expected: 201 (409 if he already exists — either way the account exists)
# @name managerSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Chidi Manager",
  "email": "chidi.manager@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234570"
}

### 2 — Setup: login the manager
# Expected: 200
# @name managerLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "chidi.manager@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 3 — Setup: login the working admin persona
# Expected: 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 4 — Admin creates a store and ASSIGNS Chidi as store admin
# Expected: 201
# @name createManaged
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Managed Branch",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{managerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "12 Market Road, Lagos",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "managed-branch@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 5 — my-store as the assigned manager
# Expected: 200 — brand "Managed Branch", storeAdminPublicId = Chidi's publicId
GET {{storeUrl}}/my-store
Authorization: Bearer {{managerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 6 — No Authorization header
# Expected: 401
GET {{storeUrl}}/my-store

### 7 — Garbage token
# Expected: 401
GET {{storeUrl}}/my-store
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-jwt

### 8 — Setup: signup the DEDICATED never-assigned admin (review round 1)
# Expected: 201 (409 if he already exists — either way the account exists)
# boss is intentionally given a store by NO probe file — see request 10.
# @name bossSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Boss Overseer",
  "email": "boss@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234574"
}

### 9 — Setup: login boss
# Expected: 200
# @name bossLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "boss@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 10 — my-store as an admin with no store
# Expected: 404 — data-gated, not role-gated. STABLE across probe files because
# boss is the one persona no file ever assigns a store to (review round 1
# finding 2: the working admin gets stores in the other files, which used to
# flip this probe's result to 200).
GET {{storeUrl}}/my-store
Authorization: Bearer {{bossLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 11 — Setup: signup a storeless persona
# Expected: 201 (409 if she already exists — either way the account exists)
# @name regularSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Bola Storeless",
  "email": "bola.storeless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031234571"
}

### 12 — Setup: login the storeless persona
# Expected: 200
# @name regularLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bola.storeless@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 13 — my-store with no store assigned
# Expected: 404 — Bola has no store; the data is the gate
GET {{storeUrl}}/my-store
Authorization: Bearer {{regularLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 14 — Wrong method: POST to my-store
# Expected: 405 — Allow: GET
POST {{storeUrl}}/my-store
Authorization: Bearer {{managerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 15 — Admin soft-deletes the managed store
# Expected: 204
DELETE {{storeUrl}}/{{createManaged.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 16 — my-store as the manager after deletion
# Expected: 200 with status DELETED — soft delete preserves history; the manager
# still sees the store, marked gone
GET {{storeUrl}}/my-store
Authorization: Bearer {{managerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
